WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.291
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 4.

2
00:00:04.911 --> 00:00:08.010
Which four values does this for loop print, one per line?

3
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:14.696
x starts at one. i equals zero: A of zero is minus zero point one.

4
00:00:14.696 --> 00:00:17.663
Is that less than minus zero point one one?

5
00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:21.047
No: minus zero point one is the bigger number.

6
00:00:21.047 --> 00:00:24.133
Is it greater than zero point one? No.

7
00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:29.000
So the else runs: x equals seven plus one over one, which is eight.

8
00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:32.887
i equals one: zero point one one is greater than

9
00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:36.909
zero point one, so x minus equals ten: minus two.

10
00:00:37.528 --> 00:00:41.892
i equals two: zero matches neither test, so the else runs again.

11
00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:47.139
But one over three is integer division, which gives zero. So x is just seven.

12
00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:51.059
i equals three: zero point two is greater than zero

13
00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:54.838
point one, so x is seven minus ten, minus three.

14
00:00:56.438 --> 00:00:58.304
Two rules decide this one.

15
00:00:58.304 --> 00:01:02.771
First, with negatives, the number closer to zero is the larger one:

16
00:01:02.771 --> 00:01:06.672
minus zero point one is greater than minus zero point one one.

17
00:01:06.672 --> 00:01:11.308
Second, when both operands are int, the slash is integer division, and

18
00:01:11.308 --> 00:01:15.379
the fraction is thrown away, even inside a double expression.

19
00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:20.244
So the loop prints eight, minus two, seven, and minus three.

20
00:01:21.063 --> 00:01:23.588
Comparing negatives backwards, or writing

21
00:01:23.588 --> 00:01:26.449
seven point three three for the third value.

22
00:01:26.449 --> 00:01:28.806
One over three in integers is zero.

23
00:01:29.526 --> 00:01:32.727
Exam tip: before tracing, circle every division in

24
00:01:32.727 --> 00:01:35.486
the code and check the types on both sides.

25
00:01:35.486 --> 00:01:37.417
int over int means truncate.
